# Implementation Plan: Equity Research Dashboard

## Overview

This document outlines the phased implementation approach for the equity research dashboard. The plan prioritizes incremental delivery, with each phase producing a working, deployable artifact.

**Total Estimated Timeline**: 3-4 weeks (part-time development)

---

## Phase 0: Foundation & Setup (Days 1-2)

### Objectives
- Set up project structure
- Configure dependencies
- Create data schema and sample JSON files
- Establish development workflow

### Tasks

#### 0.1 Project Structure Setup
- [ ] Create `/app/dashboard` directory structure
- [ ] Create `/app/dashboard/[ticker]` dynamic route
- [ ] Create `/public/data` directory
- [ ] Set up component directory: `/components/dashboard/`
- [ ] Create utility functions: `/lib/dashboard/`

#### 0.2 Dependency Installation
- [ ] Install `lightweight-charts` (TradingView)
- [ ] Install `date-fns` for date formatting
- [ ] Verify Next.js static export configuration
- [ ] Update `next.config.ts` for GitHub Pages (if needed)

#### 0.3 Data Schema & Sample Data
- [ ] Define TypeScript interfaces for data schema
- [ ] Create sample JSON files for NVDA, META, GOOG
- [ ] Populate with realistic sample data (at least 1 year of price history)
- [ ] Document data format in code comments

#### 0.4 Development Tools
- [ ] Set up TypeScript strict mode (if not already)
- [ ] Configure ESLint rules for dashboard components
- [ ] Create data validation helper (optional, for development)

### Deliverables
- ✅ Project structure in place
- ✅ Dependencies installed
- ✅ Sample data files created
- ✅ TypeScript types defined

### Engineering Decisions
- **Component Organization**: Group dashboard components in `/components/dashboard/` for clarity
- **Type Safety**: Use TypeScript interfaces for all data structures
- **Data Validation**: Skip runtime validation for MVP (assume data is correct)

